# Do Not Open Localhost in the Cursor Preview

Never open, navigate, or embed `localhost` (or `127.0.0.1`) in Cursor's in-editor browser, Simple Browser, or preview panel.

## Do Not

```text
# ❌ NEVER
Open http://localhost:5173 in Cursor Simple Browser / preview
browser_navigate to http://localhost:* or http://127.0.0.1:*
Create a Cursor browser tab just to "check the app"
```

- Do not use Cursor browser MCP tools (`browser_navigate`, `browser_tabs` with `newTab`, and the same family) against local URLs
- Do not open a preview "just to verify" UI, routing, or API changes

## What To Do Instead

- Leave the user's own browser alone; assume they already have the app open
- If verification is needed, ask the user first whether to test it on localhost. Only test after they confirm
- If you must describe a URL, write it in chat — do not launch a preview

## Allowed Exceptions

Open or test localhost only after the user confirms, either because they asked (e.g. "open localhost in Cursor", "preview this in the Simple Browser") or because you asked first and they said yes. Never start or restart the dev server for this (see the no-dev-server rule).
